    "accepted_scope": "One physically installed 20-foot liquid-cooled demonstration and GPU-testing container within the named MIRAIT ONE Shinkiba property. Completed describes the installation; no commercial operations, broader-office conversion, exact container footprint or IT MW are claimed.",
    "status_reasoning": "The original October 13 corporate article expressly says current real-equipment verification is under way and identifies the installed equipment at Shinkiba Building. It is an article based on the first September 11 video, so October 13 is a present-tense corporate confirmation, not an independent site visit, installation day or filming day. The original July 3 release already says installed and sets later operation only as a target. The packet preserves these distinctions; this supports completed installation as of October 13 under the existing confirmation-date practice.",
    "geometry_reasoning": "Both original container articles name the host Shinkiba building. The company group directory and building-occupant access page independently provide 2-15-20 Shinkiba. That access page embeds the captured Google address map, whose returned object explicitly names the MIRAIT Shinkiba Building at the address and gives 35.6393249,139.8221806. The proposed point correctly reverses axes and does not use the input viewport. Host-property scope and unknown container displacement are stated.",
    "public_copy_review": "The status summary gives a useful sourced finding and keeps demonstration/testing scope prominent. Cooling ratings remain descriptive context; neither commercial operation nor IT capacity is inferred.",
    "nonblocking_editorial_note": "In scoped_project_details.capacity_scope, “July report” refers to the July 23 Cloud Watch site report for 80 kW and three 30 kW units; making that attribution explicit would avoid confusing it with the July 3 company release. This does not affect admission.",
